# What must never reach the production image.
#
# THERE WAS NO .dockerignore, AND THE DOCKERFILE DOES `COPY backend/ /app/backend/`. That
# copies the directory as it exists on whoever's machine ran the build, which meant the built
# image contained:
#
#   backend/.env      — REAL CONFIGURATION. The copy that shipped happened to hold localhost
#                       and `.env.example` placeholders, so nothing was actually leaked. That
#                       is luck, not design: core/config.py explicitly supports backend/.env
#                       as a location, so the first person to put production values there
#                       ships the Supabase service key, the JWT secret, the model provider
#                       keys and the Razorpay secret inside a distributable artefact. An image
#                       cannot be un-shipped and the only remedy is rotating every credential.
#
#   backend/.uv_cache — 97 MB of downloaded wheel archives, INCLUDING OLD VULNERABLE COPIES of
#                       packages the image has since upgraded. This is how it was found: the
#                       Trivy gate kept reporting PyJWT 2.8.0 and cryptography 49.0.0 after
#                       both had been upgraded, because it was reading .dist-info out of the
#                       cache rather than out of site-packages. The scanner was right and the
#                       image really did contain them.
#
#   backend/.venv     — a virtualenv built for the HOST platform, with absolute paths from the
#                       host baked into its scripts. Useless in the image at best, and on an
#                       Apple-silicon machine it is the wrong architecture entirely.
#
#   .pytest_cache, .mypy_cache, .ruff_cache, .coverage, tests/ — development artefacts with no
#                       runtime purpose.
#
# DENY-LIST RATHER THAN ALLOW-LIST, deliberately: the Dockerfile copies two named directories,
# so the surface is already narrow, and an allow-list would silently drop a new package
# directory somebody adds under app/.

# ── Secrets. First, because this is the one that cannot be undone. ───────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets/

# ── Build and dependency caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.uv_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/*.egg-info

# ── Node / frontend. The backend image needs none of it. ────────────────────
node_modules
frontend
.next
out

# ── Tests and tooling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
backend/tests
**/.github
.git
.gitignore

# ── Docs, design assets and scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────
docs
design
promo
public
graphify-out
*.md
!backend/README.md
*.canvas
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
vercel.json
render.yaml
